cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results in academic work, please cite it.
  Its closest neighbours are benchmarks and papers, so someone will want to
  cite it rather than link it.
title: "context-lift: controlled context ablation for text-to-SQL agents"
abstract: >-
  A measurement framework that answers one question: does written business
  context make a text-to-SQL data agent more accurate? It runs the same gold
  questions through two arms that differ only in the authored context, scores
  them by executing both the predicted and the reference SQL, and reports a
  paired lift with an exact McNemar test, a separate safety count of answers
  the context broke, and a refusal when the question set is too small to
  resolve the effect it is being asked about.
type: software
